From 6d1b63c3a08dc1c257e85b1698a2615e586d904b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <dev@infoverify.local>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 08:04:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Birth Attestation and Newspaper Publication
 (manual-review, per reference forms)

Same manual-review pattern as NIN/BVN Modification throughout - no
provider API for either of these, so both debit the wallet, render a
submission PDF, and leave the transaction PENDING for an admin to
process by hand (NPC for attestation, BluePrint/DailyTrust for the
newspaper publication) and mark complete via the Transaction resource.

New TransactionType values: BIRTH_ATTESTATION, NEWSPAPER_PUBLICATION
(+ migration, both ADD VALUE IF NOT EXISTS in one file since neither
is referenced by the other statement in the same transaction).

Birth Attestation (birth-attestation.service.ts/.routes.ts, price
20000, single fixed field list - the reference design's own dropdown
only had one option):
- Full field set from the reference form, grouped into sections
  (Applicant, Origin & Birth, Registration, Address & Background,
  Father's Details, Mother's Details, Photo) via a new  field
  property, purely presentational - GET /fields exposes it so the
  frontend can group without duplicating the list.
- 'image' input (Upload Clean Picture) reuses the same data-URL +
  7MB-base64-cap + doc.image()-embed approach bvn-modification.service
  .ts already established for its ID card photo field.

Newspaper Publication (newspaper-publication.service.ts/.routes.ts,
price 3300, single fixed field list): old/new first/last/middle name,
split into Old Details / New Details on the PDF and the form.

Admin wiring for both: completeX/downloadXPdf action pairs on the
Transaction resource (mirrors completeBvnModification's pair exactly),
the PENDING-reversal allowlist extended, TARGET_PATH_BY_TYPE in
redirect-to-manage.tsx extended (this component fixes a real AdminJS
redirectUrl-vs-SPA-router bug - see its own comment), and a
SUPER_ADMIN-only audited PDF route per type (mirrors
admin/bvn-modification.ts), registered in admin/setup.ts.

Frontend: BirthAttestationPage.tsx (/attestation, services.ts flipped
to implemented: true) renders the field list grouped by section with
an inline consent checkbox (wording matches the reference screenshot
exactly, not a modal like NIN/BVN Modification's ModificationConsent).
NewspaperPublicationPage.tsx (/newspaper, also flipped) splits its six
fields into Old Details / New Details with its own inline confirm
checkbox. Both otherwise follow BvnModificationPage.tsx's dynamic
field-render + PIN-confirm + history/PDF-download shape.

Verified: all 173 existing backend tests still pass unchanged (vitest
run - nothing broken). Frontend tsc + vite build both clean. Backend
tsc shows the same class of stale-Prisma-client errors already present
on bvn-modification.service.ts (untouched, pre-existing file, 8 of the
same errors) - not something introduced here; this sandbox cannot run
prisma generate (binaries.prisma.sh is outside its network allowlist),
so the cached client predates schema.prisma's two new enum values.
Running prisma generate locally clears these the same way it always
has.
